		<P CLASS="ParaOverride-21" STYLE="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;margin-left:71pt;margin-top:8pt;orphans:3;text-align:justify;text-indent:-35pt;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;"><FONT CLASS="CharOverride-4" STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">(d)<FONT STYLE="width: 30px;display: inline-block;">&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;&#x00a0;</FONT>the notice or document is published on that website throughout the publication period, provided that, if the notice or document is published on that website for a part, but not all of, the publication period, the notice or document shall be treated as being published throughout that period if the failure to publish that notice of document throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have expected the Company to prevent or avoid. For the purposes of this Article 28.4 &#x201c;publication period&#x201d; means a period of not less than twenty-one days, beginning on the day on which the notification referred to in Article 28.4(c) is deemed sent.</FONT></P>
